# footprint-hold-writerless — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml).
# Axis: is anybody writing in-progress #50, and can the scan tell? Queued #60 overlaps #50 throughout.
#
# id                       | world          | patch | env | expect
# no-writer-releases       = no pod, no session, no open PR, quiet since 2026-11-13 → #60 DISPATCHES,
#                            one report line says #50's footprint left the hold set. RED on master
#                            (#60 footprint-held behind a writer-less label — the #3420 shape).
no-writer-releases         | no-writer      |       |     | no-writer-releases
# running-worker-holds     = CONTROL: a Running worker pod for #50 → #60 is still footprint-held.
running-worker-holds       | running-worker |       |     | held
# open-pr-holds            = an open PR strongly links #50 → the work is live branch state: held.
open-pr-holds              | open-pr        |       |     | held
# session-probe-fail-holds = the no-writer world, but the session-pod read fails (STUB_KUBECTL=fail):
#                            "no session" is unknown, not false → every footprint kept, #60 held.
session-probe-fail-holds   | no-writer      |       | STUB_KUBECTL=fail | session-probe-fail-holds
# recent-holds             = the no-writer world, #50 touched "now" (inside C4C5_PERSIST_S): the
#                            label-write → pod-create window never releases → held.
recent-holds               | no-writer      | gh/issue-list-inprog.json @ patches/recent.jq | | held
# error-label-holds        = the no-writer world, #50 also `agent/error`: a human owns it → held.
error-label-holds          | no-writer      | gh/issue-list-inprog.json @ patches/agent-error.jq | | held
